# 💬 Toxic Comment Classification

A beginner-level **Natural Language Processing (NLP)** project that classifies online comments as **Toxic** or **Non-Toxic** using **TF-IDF** and **Multinomial Naive Bayes**.

The project also includes a simple **Streamlit web application** where users can enter a comment and receive an instant classification.

---

## 📌 Problem Statement

Online platforms receive a large number of comments every day. Some comments may contain insults, offensive language, or toxic expressions.

Manually identifying these comments can be difficult when dealing with large amounts of text.

This project uses **Natural Language Processing and Machine Learning** to automatically classify comments into:

* ⚠️ **Toxic**
* ✅ **Non-Toxic**

---

## 🎯 Project Objectives

* Understand the basics of **NLP text classification**
* Clean and preprocess text data
* Convert text into numerical features using **TF-IDF**
* Train a **Multinomial Naive Bayes** classifier
* Evaluate the model using classification metrics
* Build a simple **Streamlit application** for real-time prediction

---

## 🧠 Technologies Used

* Python
* Pandas
* NumPy
* Scikit-learn
* NLTK
* Matplotlib
* Streamlit
* Joblib

---

## 🔄 Project Workflow

```text
Online Comments
       ↓
Data Cleaning
       ↓
Text Preprocessing
       ↓
TF-IDF Feature Extraction
       ↓
Multinomial Naive Bayes
       ↓
Model Evaluation
       ↓
Toxic / Non-Toxic
       ↓
Streamlit Web App
```

